# Line endings are pinned to LF so a file's bytes do not depend on the contributor's
# core.autocrlf or on which editor last saved it. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# autocrlf=true rewrites every .rs file on commit and the diff shows whole-file rewrites
# instead of one changed line.
#
# Rust sources: rustfmt and clippy do not care, but a mixed-ending file makes every later
# diff unreadable, and that is the cost this line removes.
*.rs text eol=lf

# Cards, docs and backlog are generated and compared as text.
*.md text eol=lf

# Pinned so the lockfile does not churn between platforms.
Cargo.lock text eol=lf

# Nothing is needed for build output: `target/` is already gitignored, so no build artifact
# is ever a candidate for normalisation.
